  "full_text": "**\n\nWait, the solution says the ball costs 10 cents. But it seems like it's comparing the total cost. Let me think again.\n\nWait, if the bat is one dollar more than the ball, that would make the ball 5 cents, and the bat 105 cents. But then the total would be 110. Hmm, maybe that's right. So why did I think it's 10? Maybe I confused something.\n\nWait, perhaps I misread the question. Let me check again. It says the bat and ball cost one dollar and ten cents in total. The bat costs one dollar more than the ball. So, mathematically, if the ball is \\( b \\) cents, then the bat is \\( b + 100 \\) cents. So total is \\( b + (b + 100) = 110 \\). So, \\( 2b + 100 = 110 \\), subtract 100: \\( 2b = 10 \\), so \\( b = 5 \\). So actually, the ball is 5 cents, not 10. Maybe I did the math wrong earlier"
